ÄÄF1ÄÄÁÄÄF2ÄÄÄÁÄÄF3ÄÄÄÁÄÄF4ÄÄÄÁÄÄF5ÄÄÄÁÄÄF6ÄÄÄÁÄÄF7ÄÄÄÁÄÄF8ÄÄÄÁÄÄF9ÄÄÁÄF10ÄÁ
Beams.  (U.G. 12,  Ref. 69-70)
F1-4 1B, 2B, 3B, 4B : automatically beam in groups of 1, 2, 3 or 4 eighth
                      notes of total rhythm.  (U.G. 12)

 **** At least one note number must be given BEFORE clicking on F5,6,7.*****
F5  ÄÄ5ÄÄ : Quintuplet number on beam - adds 500 to note number.  Sets P8.
F6  ÄÄ6ÄÄ : Sextuplet number on beam - adds 600 to note number.   
F7  ÄÄ3ÄÄ : Triplet num. on beam - adds 300 to note number. (U.G. 53, Ref. 73)
F8  Go    : Go finish, ignore this prompt and the following 'Slurs' prompt.
F9  <esc>
 ***** F10, <alt>F10 must be clicked BEFORE any note numbers are given.*****
F10      Above : puts + in front of note number - bracket is above notes.
<alt>F10 Below : puts - in front of note number - bracket is below notes.

<alt>F1,2,3 Pkup : 
 *** For pick-ups, <alt>F1,2,3 must be clicked BEFORE clicking on F1-4.****
 *** Click here to start automatic beaming after 1, 2 or 3 notes. (Ref. 69-70)      
<alt>F5 AutoBms : Beam groups according to meter. (2/4=2B, 6/8=3B, etc.)
